# Independent native Kafka fixture, source-only handoff

Root must review all three sources and grant native execution separately. No
broker pull or execution, compiler, Java, fixture or verifier run has occurred
from this handoff. The root's accepted test-only attribution supplement remains
separate from the original incomplete acquisition inventory and wrong notice.

`kafka-native.ts` owns Testcontainers12.1.0 lifecycle and serial in-container
commands. `kafka-native-launch.py` owns the host hard deadline, frozen inputs,
bounded output parsing and exact emergency retirement. `kafka-admission/native_verify.py`
independently verifies original wire/Java output bytes, without production code.
It imports only the frozen independent manifest/probe sources. Those original
sources and both Java sources remain unchanged.

The exact Kafka arm64 child is
`apache/kafka@sha256:77b56ddfb7104fc5814a3d0127fcff49983220c7c7ad9bfc1f0af4d439228329`,
expected actual image/config ID
`sha256:8e12eba3b69e43eeed26ccf9072d46f3fe38ce0c7f5ffe66d7d9b6198801f5cc`.
The image must be separately pulled/admitted before this gate. There is no
explicit pull command and Testcontainers pull policy is false; an exact cached
image is required first. If another task deletes the image during this race,
stop rather than accepting an acquisition as this gate's intended operation.

The outer owner requires an explicit compiler directory and exact qualification SHA.
The fixture verifies clean compile exit/noOOM/retirement, every recorded class
hash/size/version61 and both roots, then exact copied compiler-input JAR hashes.
For the actual first attempt, the pinned recovery SHA
`eeca0a794b96ee7ae6a5fa9fbfbaaf85735ba72a671a5a51d009994ab21461ba`
selects only `recovery.json` and `classes-recovered`. This mode verifies the exact
original failed terminal SHA, exact inputs/source/archive/parser SHA, unchanged
zero compiler exit/noOOM/retirement, and the sole original inspect/copy ValueError.
It admits exactly11 recovered class names/30389B, then verifies every class hash
and the two original Java source hashes. Any other original failure refuses.
It preserves the original failed terminal; it neither ignores all cleanup faults
nor treats a recovery receipt as evidence of Java class execution.
No wildcard classpath or discovery of arbitrary plugin/logging directories.
One unique attempt directory records fixed original append/fetch inputs and CRC
input before starting a broker. Topic/partition/timestamps/offsets are planned
before native output exists, never reconstructed from candidate decoding.

Proposed invocation after root source/native GO:

```sh
python3 .tmp/implementation/kafka-native-launch.py first /Users/okikio/Other/Code/opfs/.tmp/implementation/opfs-kafka-compile-first eeca0a794b96ee7ae6a5fa9fbfbaaf85735ba72a671a5a51d009994ab21461ba
```

Host Node is the existing explicit26.13.0 arm64 binary, heap256MiB; its binary
SHA/version/path and host Python identity are retained. Node heap is not a total
RSS guarantee. Native container ceiling is1GiB memory=swap, CPU1/PID128, no host
mounts/credentials/capability additions, cap-dropALL/no-new-privileges. One
Testcontainers network and one labelled broker are owned. Ryuk/reuse are disabled
so no second resource container can appear. Testcontainers readiness remains the
startup authority; its failure boundary retains actual state/logs before library
automatic removal. The outer owner repairs only exact labelled leftovers.

The broker uses256MiB heap; format/readiness/topic CLI and Java oracles use128MiB
heap inside that same container, serially. Broker plus one auxiliary JVM may run;
two auxiliary JVMs never overlap. Fixed env-i removes credentials/proxies/tool
options from Java, and startup overrides the image's default entrypoint. Kafka
image runtime classes are necessary for official broker/CLI use and are outside
the five-JAR client-only closure; this native gate requires that explicit root
acceptance, not an assertion that only five JARs execute anywhere.

All image volumes are replaced by owned tmpfs: data32MiB, tmp8MiB, broker file
logs1MiB, secrets/config64KiB each. Docker console rotation1MiB/one file.
TMPFS extents and isolation are checked before engine start and again afterward.
Small fixed segment/index/retention/request limits bound the planned one-topic
workload; tmpfs is the physical ceiling, not a claim that retention is a quota.
The unproven32MiB data/PID128/readiness profile may fail; preserve actual evidence
before proposing any resource change. Snapshot actual `du` and pre-stop state.

Actual native-first stopped during format with ConfigException: the Kafka4.4.0
minimum metadata.log.segment.bytes is8388608. The revised source sets exactly
8MiB; data tmpfs stays32MiB. The one user partition still has1MiB segment/index
settings and two three-record writes of roughly132KiB each. Metadata bootstrap,
checkpoint/snapshot and index files also share that32MiB, so an8MiB segment
ceiling is not a total storage estimate or proof of allocated file extents.
Format failed before useful actual directory measurements; metadata index and
bootstrap overhead are not yet quantified. There is no observed ENOSPC or other
evidence requiring a larger physical ceiling. Retain32MiB for the next bounded
attempt, inspect its actual storage receipt, and treat any exhaustion as a real
failure requiring a separate evidence-based budget decision. No storage expansion
is included in this repair.

Actual native-second completed its broker/SDK/literal sequence in15.25s with
zero native exit/noOOM/fixture faults and confirmed retirement. Its measured data
was304KiB, tmp184KiB and retained results152KiB, so32MiB was sufficient for this
specific bounded run. The independent semantic verifier then refused its own
incorrect timestamp label. KafkaOracle.java206 deliberately writes
`record.timestampType().name()`. The pinned upstream enum at
`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/apache/kafka/1156b2752aaa28eafc0b4c4d387e63356793268d/clients/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/record/TimestampType.java`
(retained `kafka-admission/TimestampType.java`, SHA
`89e55d22dd3bfa0d2090ca0fd8a2b35dd5f1cb14bbbdbdc1c07964b4336484f8`)
declares enum constant CREATE_TIME and a distinct display-name field CreateTime;
toString returns that display field. The narrow verifier fix expects CREATE_TIME,
with no native/source/JAR/input changes. Root can replay only the pure verifier
over exact retained native-second outputs; original terminal failure remains
unchanged and any subsequent semantic recovery proof must be separate. Final
SDK full-byte and JDK CRC assertions remain pending that replay.

On startup failure, Testcontainers can remove the container before start rejects.
The revised owner accepts already-removed status only with structured Docker404,
matching retained readiness-state identity/label and bounded log, and an exact
empty container-ID query. It records that attributed retirement and skips duplicate
inspect/remove calls. Any other inspection failure remains a cleanup fault.
Primary startup failure remains separately recorded, even when retirement was
successful. Readiness and broker log capture now retain both Docker stdout and
stderr within the same1MiB combined retained limit; the first ConfigException
was preserved in native.log while its separate readiness.log was empty.

Only EXTERNAL9094 is dynamically published to127.0.0.1. INTERNAL9092 and
CONTROLLER9093 listen on container loopback only. The Testcontainers starting
hook obtains the actual mapped port and publishes one fixed generated properties
file atomically through an owned bounded exec before a waiting bootstrap starts
Kafka. Class/JAR/original input source copies all precede engine start. Metadata
advertises the exact external endpoint for the probe and container loopback for
the Java oracle. No arbitrary advertised address is followed.

Sequence: format, broker/readiness, explicit one-partition topic creation with
auto-create disabled/CreateTime/uncompressed; official Java append; original
literal probe fetch at0; literal probe append/fetch at3; official Java fetch at3;
JDK CRC32C over the exact original literal batch CRC input. Request/response
frames retain correlations, full original bytes, hashes and independent receipt.
No OPFS candidate is imported. Later production code must replay these original
frames and repeat both native directions; this gate alone is independent oracle
qualification, not production provider coverage or CI completion.

The verifier requires actual SDK acknowledgment offsets0,1,2 and timestamps;
Produce3 response error=0/baseOffset3; ListOffsets1 original offsets; Fetch4
CRC32C, uncompressed magic2 batches and full original null/empty keys/values,
binary values, ordered duplicate headers and timestamp/offset deltas; and actual
Java fetch equality at3,4,5. It separately checks Java builtin CRC32C agreement.
Metadata4 is framing/correlation captured, not yet independently semantically
decoded. SDK poll max-records is not the candidate's whole-wire-page overflow
proof. Unknown append on killed/incomplete native stages remains conservative;
the raw probe does not manufacture semantic acknowledgments from framing.

Host deadline180s, readiness90s, individual CLI30s/oracle45s, each probe50s and
CRC15s. Host native log4MiB; semantic output1MiB; original wire frames4MiB each.
Oracle files first live in8MiB tmpfs. Before stop, an owned shell snapshots only
known result basenames, each at its admitted maximum plus one byte, into the
owned writable home directory. This retains finite failure evidence across
tmpfs teardown; oversize is refused by the outer parser, never silently passed.
Copy only after stopped-state admission: SDK stdout4MiB, stderr1MiB, physical
single-file tar parser rejects aliases/extensions/path/padding/appended members.
No host extractall or filesystem symlink traversal. Full output identities and
semantic terminal results are distinct from primary/cleanup/container outcomes.

Root must recheck image pull headroom and existing128MiB research reserve before
native GO. The outer currently conservatively requires1500MiB+512MiB free; it is
not a filesystem quota or an instruction to delete unrelated resources. Peak
additional native tmpfs41.125MiB, fixed oracle/class copies<=28MiB and retained
known-file snapshot<=15MiB coexist with host evidence/input copies. Existing
retention must be counted, rather than assuming those totals fit the reserve.
Compiler image retirement and Kafka pull admission remain separately owned gates.
